{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether adding image information at all is beneficial in this multimodal cellular profiling task. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal, clean extension of the baseline: it keeps the same profile setting (singleprofile) and RNA encoder (pca_n2000), adds a standard ResNet50 image encoder, and uses the simplest fusion (concat). This directly tests the core hypothesis of the study—does the image modality contribute complementary signal beyond RNA?—while changing the fewest possible variables. If multimodal significantly outperforms the 48.5% baseline, we gain strong evidence to invest remaining budget in optimizing image encoders, fusion strategies, and multiprofile aggregation. If it does not, we learn early that the image branch is not helping and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder upgrades (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. Under a tight budget with near-zero evidence, resolving this top-level design question is far more informative than tuning secondary choices (aggregation, fusion type, or encoder variant) within a modality whose value we have not yet established."
}

